;; wire-requirements.edn — the 27 ARGUE'd requirements as WIRES.
;;
;; Joe, 2026-09-19: warrants certify only needed behaviour, required for
;; running the machine; the real "wires" of the system are what gets tested
;; and warranted. The 27 requirements (ARGUE-realness-requirements-2026-09-19)
;; "are either types of wires, or individual instances of wires, and all
;; should be reviewable and queriable."
;;
;; :wire-form :instance — one producer→consumer seam (an edge, drawn or owed).
;; :wire-form :type     — a duty that holds across every wire of a class
;;                        (retention, identity, independence, recording).
;; :wires — R-node edge(s) from the control map where the seam has one, else
;;          a named seam. Classifications are claude-12 drafts (2026-09-19)
;;          for review; the ARGUE basis column is claude-4's, verified.
;; :subject-id — the test-registry subject that warrants this wire; nil means
;;          not yet bound (the gap list).
;;
;; Queriable via: bb scripts/wire_register.bb  (joins this file with
;; p4ng/empirics-futon/aif-conformance.edn and the live subjects ledger).

